WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.367
-Amid a national outcry
for stricter gun safety measures

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.367
to stop America's plague
of mass shootings,

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:09.033
pro-gun politicians
who refuse to take action

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.033
are pitching
an insane alternative.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.467
Instead of getting rid of guns,
they want to get rid of doors.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.868
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.367
This should be blindingly
obvious to anyone

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.767
with clear eyes
and a conscience,

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.634
but America has
more mass shootings

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.367
than any peer nation
in the world

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.701
because we have more guns

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.901
than any other peer nation
in the world.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.234
Study after study after study
has proven that,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.167
although I'm not sure
we need a study

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:38.834
to confirm what we can all see
with our own eyes.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.501
It's common sense --
common sense to everyone,

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.834
apparently,
except for the craven ghouls

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.167
who refuse to even acknowledge
America's gun crisis.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:47.801
In fact, those guys
have a different idea

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.367
for stopping mass shootings --

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.868
just get rid of doors.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.234
-We have to harden these targets

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.067
so no one can get in ever

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.501
except through one entrance.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.934
Maybe that would would help.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.567
Maybe that would stop someone.

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:02.033
-One of the things
that everyone agreed

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.901
is don't have all of these
unlocked back doors,

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:08.234
have one door into
and out of the school,

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.567
and have that one door --

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.300
armed police officers
at that door.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.968
-I'm sorry,
you don't want gun control,

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:16.501
but you want door control?!
Are you...

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.067
Are you ins--
Why not stop at one?

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.868
Why not just outlaw doors
altogether?

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.767
Then no one would need keys
to get in your house.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.000
You'd just have to climb up
to the roof

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.167
and slide headfirst
down the chimney.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:28.000
Really? You really think
one door is a good idea?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.801
Then how about you try it first?
One door for the Senate,

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.901
and you can all line up
to go in every day,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.868
which Ted Cruz might
not think is bad,

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.367
but it's a [bleep] nightmare

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.968
for whoever has to stand
next to Ted Cruz.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.701
"You know, this
one-door thing was my idea."

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.033
"Can we not?"

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.300
Just spitballing here,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.100
but maybe run this idea
by a fire marshal first

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.534
and see what they have
to say about it.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:53.200
Because famously,
nothing bad has ever happened

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.534
when there's only one way in

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.501
and one way out
of a crowded building.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.234
Can you imagine
what would happen

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.567
if someone in an office, say,

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.334
with only one door
yelled "fire"?

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.734
Or worse still,

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:04.634
"Ted Cruz is in the break room"?

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.868
These obviously
aren't serious ideas.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.100
They're pathetic excuses

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.901
from the most depraved people
in our politics

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.968
who would rather do the bidding
of powerful forces like the NRA

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:16.100
than do anything to stop
these massacres from happening.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.734
In fact, Cruz and Donald Trump,
among others,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:23.567
are still scheduled to address
an NRA event in Texas on Friday.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.434
These people would rather talk
about door control

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.868
than the obvious answers
that have worked

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.434
in other peer nations
across the world,

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:31.267
from Australia to the UK
to Norway to New Zealand,

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.601
and that's to regulate guns.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:34.400
And by the way,
when we've done it here,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.234
like the 1994 assault weapons
ban, it worked, too.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:39.968
We have too many guns,
and they're too easy to get,

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.467
and it's as simple as that.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.534
And it's sickening
and rage-inducing

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:44.868
that people
in positions of power

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.534
just ignore
those obvious truths,

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:47.868
no matter how loud we say them,

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.567
which might be
why Beto O'Rourke,

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.434
the Democratic candidate
for governor in Texas,

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.400
interrupted
a press conference yesterday

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.901
to tell Texas Governor
Greg Abbott directly,

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.834
in a way that Abbott
could not ignore,

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.501
that something must be done now

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.534
to stop these horrific events
from happening again.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.667
And Cruz, who was there as well,

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.467
could not help but respond

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.701
while displaying an astonishing
lack of self-awareness.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.734
-Texas gubernatorial candidate
Beto O'Rourke interrupted

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.334
Governor Abbott's
press conference,

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.467
saying yesterday's shooting was,
quote, "totally predictable"

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.334
and talking to reporters
afterward,

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:21.501
blaming Abbott for refusing
to strengthen gun laws.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.834
-Excuse me. Sit down.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.400
You're out --
you're out of line,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.868
and an embarrassment.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:32.000
-I'm sorry, Ted Cruz
is accusing someone else

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.367
of pulling a stunt?

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.767
This is the same guy who read
"Green Eggs and Ham"

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.434
on the Senate floor,

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:40.000
released a campaign ad
where he used a machine gun

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.501
to fry bacon,
and posted a video of himself

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.601
lurking in the bushes
at the Rio Grande

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:47.467
like he was auditioning
for a role on "Duck Dynasty."

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.834
He looks like he's being filmed
for a nature documentary

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.167
on the BBC.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.334
[ British accent ] A rare
sighting of the bearded coward

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.467
indigenous to these parts

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.133
until he makes his annual
flight south for the winter.

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:02.801
Listen, listen to the sound
of his rolly suitcase

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:05.767
across the linoleum,
which experts say

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.267
is his way of telling predators,
"I suck, I suck.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:11.033
If you eat me,
you'll probably puke."

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.968
[ Normal voice ] And then,
in a pretty stunning exchange,

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:16.734
Ted Cruz was confronted
by a reporter for Sky News

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:20.634
about why these kind of horrific
events only happen in America.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.667
And since Cruz had no answer,

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.300
aside from the obvious one he
doesn't want to discuss -- guns,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.200
he angrily stormed off.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.968
-Is this the moment
to reform gun laws?

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.367
-You know, it's easy
to go to politics.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.400
-But it's important.
It's at the heart of the issue.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.734
-I get that that's where
the media likes to go.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.434
-No, it's not.
It's where many of the people

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:40.267
we've talked to here like to go.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.267
-You got your political agenda.
-No, it's honestly --

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:43.734
-God love you.
-Senator, It's not.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.067
I just want to understand

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.400
why you do not think
that guns are the problem.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.801
-Why is this just
an American problem?

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.834
-It is just
an American problem, sir.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.334
-Mr. Cruz, why is America

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.400
the only country
that faces this kind of --

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.901
-You know what?
-...mass shooting?

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.067
-But you can't answer that. You
can't answer that, can you, sir?

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.601
You can't answer that.
Why is this country --

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:03.267
-Why is it that people come from
all over the world to America?

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:06.234
'Cause it's the freest, most
prosperous, safest country on

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.234
Earth, and stop the propaganda.
-It may be the freest --

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:10.067
It may be the most --
-Why are our kids dying

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.734
in schools, Mr. Cruz?

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.067
-Man, look at him run away.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.200
I bet he was thankful that place
had more than one door.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.701
"We got more?"

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.567
"Alright, we're good."

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:25.367
Cruz had no answer
because the obvious one,

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.767
the number and easy availability

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.634
of military-grade weapons
in this country,

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.033
is one he doesn't
want to discuss.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:33.601
In his case, he's choosing
the ludicrous idea

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:35.868
of door control
as a distraction.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.934
But in other cases,
pro-gun Republicans

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.834
just admit they don't
want to do anything.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.734
Like when Colorado
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:44.400
tweeted yesterday, "You cannot
legislate away evil."

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.033
Or when Texas Attorney General
Ken Paxton said this.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:49.567
-We can't stop bad people
from doing bad things.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.200
They're gonna violate
murder laws,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.367
they're not gonna
follow gun laws.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:54.033
I've never understood
that argument.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.634
-"Laws don't work" is a hell
of a thing to hear from somebody

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:59.367
whose job description
is to make or enforce laws.

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:04.067
At least, at least the weirdos
in the New Age store believe

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:06.834
that the $40 crystals
they're selling actually work.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.534
By the way, they don't.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.601
Either that
or I'm sitting on 'em wrong.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:14.734
Also, stop hiding behind
the bull[bleep] talking point

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:17.801
that calling for gun control
is somehow politicizing tragedy

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:19.434
and that there's
nothing lawmakers can do.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:21.167
First of all,
you guys are the ones

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.100
using politics
to loosen gun laws.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.100
Second, what else
is politics for

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.801
if not to deal
with a crisis like this?

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:28.534
That's what our political system
is supposed to do.

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:30.501
You're a lawmaker. If you don't
want to do your job,

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:32.300
then just go back
to the [bleep] bushes

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.467
to live with the other Bigfoots.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:37.534
[ As Cruz ] Hello, fellow
Bigfoots, I'm Ted Cruz.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:40.200
[ Growls ]

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.968
[ Gruffly ] Bigfoot need door
to get away from this man.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:46.067
[ Normal voice] This is why
it was so cathartic

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.567
for so many people
to see someone

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.467
just directly confront
the people in power

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.801
who refuse to take action
because so often they behave

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:53.734
as though
they can simply ignore us.

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:56.033
They act like they don't
have to care what we think

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:57.834
or how we feel,
like they're totally immune

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.567
from accountability
and public opinion.

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.267
And that's because
this is a political party

00:07:01.267 --> 00:07:02.634
that sees itself as insulated

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:04.834
from public accountability
and popular opinion.

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:06.133
I mean, measures

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:07.200
like background checks

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.701
and assault weapons bans,

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:09.701
which should be

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:10.767
the bare minimum,

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:12.167
are massively popular

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:13.234
across political lines.

00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:14.801
And yet pro-gun politicians

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.167
and the powerful interests
behind them simply do not care.

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:18.901
They think democracy
does not apply to them.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:21.000
That's why they want
to cheat in elections

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.868
and dismantle democracy on guns
or any other issue.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:26.300
They just do not see themselves

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.634
as accountable
to public opinion.

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:29.534
I mean, for God's sake,
we just found out yesterday

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:32.033
that on the day of an attempted
coup to overturn an election,

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.968
the outgoing president
reacted approvingly

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:37.567
when he heard the mob
was chanting "Hang Mike Pence."

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:39.601
Trump's former chief of staff,
Mark Meadows,

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:41.534
reportedly told colleagues
that Trump had said

00:07:41.534 --> 00:07:43.400
maybe Pence should be hanged.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.367
And somehow we're all
supposed to just, like,

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.200
move on from that.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.601
I saw that headline yesterday,
let out a long sigh,

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:51.367
and then just
had to keep scrolling.

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.501
Then I did -- I will admit
I did laugh a little,

00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:55.467
thinking about some time
in the future

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:56.934
when Pence tries
to be diplomatic

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.133
to appeal to Trump's base
and says something like,

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:01.634
"President Trump and I
don't always see eye to eye.

00:08:01.634 --> 00:08:05.801
For example, I thought
hanging me was a bad idea."

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:10.334
"Different strokes."

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:11.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:13.133
This is, of course, the same guy

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:15.467
who famously tried to steal
the election in Georgia

00:08:15.467 --> 00:08:18.200
by shaking down the secretary
of state like a mob boss.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.701
So, after that attempt failed,

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:21.400
Trump quickly
developed a vendetta

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.367
against Georgia's statewide
Republican officials,

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:25.167
including the guy
on that phone call,

00:08:25.167 --> 00:08:27.100
Secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger,

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.534
and Governor Brian Kemp.

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:30.834
And by the way, neither of
these guys are secret liberals.

00:08:30.834 --> 00:08:32.200
Raffensperger has supported

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.701
voter suppression efforts
in the state,

00:08:33.701 --> 00:08:36.033
and Kemp is such
a rock-ribbed conservative,

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.767
he once aired this actual
television ad.

00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:41.000
-I'm Brian Kemp.
I'm so conservative...

00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:45.300
...I blow up
government spending.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.200
My chainsaw's ready to rip up
some regulations.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.200
[ Motor revs ]

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.968
I got a big truck
just in case

00:08:52.968 --> 00:08:54.801
I need to round up
criminal illegals

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.133
and take 'em home myself.

00:08:56.133 --> 00:08:57.133
[ Engine starts ]

00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:59.300
Yep, I just said that.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.601
-Cool.

00:09:00.601 --> 00:09:03.834
He's got the same slogan
as a [bleep] standup comic

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:05.667
who thinks he's being edgy
by telling jokes

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:07.434
about how millennials
are pampered.

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:10.767
"Oh, yeah. How about instead
of whining about student loans,

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:13.734
you stop spending 12 bucks
on avocado toast?

00:09:13.734 --> 00:09:17.000
Yeah... I just said that."

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.334 --> 00:09:20.701
Also, where'd you guys go
for that kick-ass explosion?

00:09:20.701 --> 00:09:23.200
Steven Seagal's House
of Discount Special Effects?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.701
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.701 --> 00:09:25.934
I may be...

00:09:25.934 --> 00:09:27.100
[ Deep voice ] I may be...
[ Laughs ]

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.334
[ Normal voice ] Sorry, I forgot
I have to do Steven Seagal.

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:31.667
No, shh, shh!

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:33.968
We're gonna edit this out,
gonna go to full frame,

00:09:33.968 --> 00:09:36.767
and then just come right out
like I knew what was coming.

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:38.601
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.601 --> 00:09:40.934
Okay, so remember,
I just said Steven Seagal...

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.934 --> 00:09:43.334
Now...
[ Laughs ]

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:44.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.467
No, no! Shh, shh!
It has to...

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:48.300
No, it has to feel really real.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.801
[ Laughs ]

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.133 --> 00:09:54.934
[ Deep voice ]
I may be above the law,

00:09:54.934 --> 00:09:57.434
but my prices
are below the competition.

00:09:57.434 --> 00:09:58.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.434 --> 00:10:00.567
[ Normal voice ]
And yet -- and yet,

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:03.467
because Kemp and Raffensperger
refused to commit election fraud

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:05.200
and singlehandedly
overturn the results,

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.100
Trump pursued personal vendettas
against them

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.467
by recruiting and endorsing
primary challengers

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:10.834
who embraced his big lie.

00:10:10.834 --> 00:10:12.567
It's the same thing
that happened in Pennsylvania,

00:10:12.567 --> 00:10:14.300
where a pro-coup candidate

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.267
who wanted to overturn
that state's results in 2020

00:10:17.267 --> 00:10:19.200
is now the GOP nominee
for governor there.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.667
Only in Georgia,
Trump's plan didn't work.

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:24.501
Going into the election,
Kemp's challenger, David Perdue,

00:10:24.501 --> 00:10:27.400
was already down double digits
despite Trump's endorsement,

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.534
although he refused, of course,
to accept that reality.

00:10:30.534 --> 00:10:32.801
-You are down by 30 percentage
points in the polls.

00:10:32.801 --> 00:10:34.133
What's happened
to your campaign?

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:35.934
-Well, first of all,
where'd you get the 30 points?

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:37.000
-Fox News poll.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.501
-Right.
Where'd they get it from?

00:10:39.501 --> 00:10:41.000
-Are you not down 30 points?
-No, no, no. No.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.667
Hell no, I'm not down 30 points.

00:10:42.667 --> 00:10:44.334
-In a way, he was right.

00:10:44.334 --> 00:10:46.501
Currently, he's down
by 50 points.

00:10:46.501 --> 00:10:47.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.834 --> 00:10:49.901
[ As Perdue ] Hell no,
I'm not down 30 points!

00:10:49.901 --> 00:10:51.801
I wish!

00:10:51.801 --> 00:10:54.467
I'd give my right arm
to be within 30 points.

00:10:54.467 --> 00:10:56.067
You see that guy
I'm running against?

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:58.300
Got explosions, a chainsaw,
a big old truck.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.534
I wish I was that guy!

00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:02.234
Instead, I'm a big old drip."

00:11:02.234 --> 00:11:03.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.634 --> 00:11:05.267
[ Normal voice ] The Republican
Party and the gun lobby

00:11:05.267 --> 00:11:06.434
see themselves as immune

00:11:06.434 --> 00:11:07.901
to democracy
and public opinion,

00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:11.667
which is why they don't care
that large majorities of people

00:11:11.667 --> 00:11:13.968
want stricter gun safety laws.

00:11:13.968 --> 00:11:16.033
They think they can just
brazenly ignore voters

00:11:16.033 --> 00:11:18.033
and still hold on to power
by cheating.

00:11:18.033 --> 00:11:20.067
That's part of why
this all feels so frustrating

00:11:20.067 --> 00:11:21.534
and infuriating
and rage-inducing.

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:24.367
These people don't think
they have to care

00:11:24.367 --> 00:11:26.067
what we the American people
want.

00:11:26.067 --> 00:11:28.534
But as we discussed
at length yesterday,

00:11:28.534 --> 00:11:30.634
other countries
and our own history

00:11:30.634 --> 00:11:33.567
have shown us time and again
that we can change things.

00:11:33.567 --> 00:11:36.601
We can stop these horrors.
We have that power.

00:11:36.601 --> 00:11:38.133
It hasn't always been like this,

00:11:38.133 --> 00:11:39.400
doesn't always have
to be like this.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.934
Pro-gun politicians

00:11:40.934 --> 00:11:43.234
and the entrenched
special interests behind them

00:11:43.234 --> 00:11:44.934
can try to ignore us
all they want,

00:11:44.934 --> 00:11:46.601
but we must keep at it,

00:11:46.601 --> 00:11:48.501
whether it's calling
one lawmaker

00:11:48.501 --> 00:11:51.234
or making one donation
or knocking on...

00:11:51.234 --> 00:11:52.567
-One door.

00:11:52.567 --> 00:11:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.801 --> 00:11:58.467
-This has been "A Closer Look."

